- `GET /api/v1/recognition-jobs/:id`
- `POST /api/v1/recognition-jobs/:id/cancel` where cancellation is supported
- `GET /api/v1/pages/:id/transcriptions`

Support:

- Line-level recognition
- Full-page recognition only if a suitable segmentation workflow exists
- Language selection
- Model selection where authorized
- Job status tracking
- Model metadata
- Processing duration
- Failure reporting

Use these job statuses:

- QUEUED
- PROCESSING
- COMPLETED
- FAILED
- CANCELLED

Long-running jobs must not block ordinary API requests indefinitely.

Use a simple database-backed job worker or another appropriately scoped mechanism for the first implementation.

Prevent the same queued job from being processed multiple times concurrently.

Handle backend restarts and interrupted jobs safely.

Set request timeouts and handle unavailable AI services.

Save the original model output and model metadata.

Do not fabricate confidence scores.

